# Vercel Web Analytics Configuration Report

## Summary
Vercel Web Analytics was already properly installed and configured in this project. After fetching the latest documentation from https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart, I verified that the implementation follows the current best practices for Next.js App Router projects.

## Current Implementation Status

### Package Installation
- ✅ `@vercel/analytics` version 2.0.1 is already installed in package.json
- ✅ Dependencies are properly resolved in pnpm-lock.yaml

### Configuration
- ✅ Analytics component is imported from `@vercel/analytics/next` (correct path for Next.js)
- ✅ Component is placed in the root layout at `src/app/(frontend)/layout.tsx`
- ✅ Component is positioned at the end of the `<body>` tag (recommended placement)

### Implementation Details
The Analytics component is correctly implemented in the root layout file:

**File:** `src/app/(frontend)/layout.tsx`
- Import statement: `import { Analytics } from "@vercel/analytics/next"`
- Component usage: `<Analytics />` at the end of body tag (line 89)

This follows the official Vercel documentation for Next.js App Router integration exactly.

